---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { buildSEOMeta, getHubUrl } from '../../../lib/seoEngine';

const lang = 'en';
const title = 'Time Tracking for Freelancers: The Ultimate Guide 2026';
const description = 'Maximize your billable hours. Learn how to track time efficiently as a freelancer, calculate hourly rates, and avoid common billing mistakes.';

const seo = buildSEOMeta(
  lang,
  {},
  '/en/guides/tracking-time-freelancers/',
  'de',
  '/ratgeber/zeiterfassung-freelancer/'
);

const hubUrl = getHubUrl(lang);
---

<BaseLayout 
  title={seo.title}
  description={seo.description}
  canonical={seo.canonical}
  hreflang={seo.hreflang}
  lang={lang}
>
  <article class="guide-content">
    <header class="guide-header">
      <nav class="breadcrumb">
        <a href={hubUrl}>Home</a> › <a href="/en/guides/">Guides</a> › Freelancer Time Tracking
      </nav>
      <h1>{title}</h1>
      <p class="lead">For freelancers, time is literally money. If you don't track your hours with precision, you're essentially giving away your income every month. Let's optimize your workflow.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="glass-card content-card">
      <section>
        <h2>1. The Cost of "Guess-timation"</h2>
        <p>Many independent professionals wait until the end of the day or week to estimate their billable time. Studies show that "retroactive tracking" can miss up to 25% of actual billable work — such as quick client calls, urgent emails, or research phases.</p>
        <div class="tip-box">
          <strong>Expert Tip:</strong> Use our <a href={hubUrl}>Time Calculator</a> to instantly convert small time increments into billable decimals for your invoices.
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Billing Units: Hours vs. Days</h2>
        <p>Depending on your contract, you may bill by <strong>hourly rates</strong> or <strong>day rates</strong>. A standard day rate usually assumes 8 hours of work. If you work 10 hours, you should bill 1.25 units to ensure fairness.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. The 60/20/20 Rule for Productivity</h2>
        <p>A balanced freelancer day consists of more than just billable work:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>60% Billable Work:</strong> Core project delivery.</li>
          <li><strong>20% Marketing & Sales:</strong> Finding the next project.</li>
          <li><strong>20% Admin & Overhead:</strong> Invoicing, learning, and emails.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Conclusion: Precision Wins</h2>
        <p>Regardless of the tool you use, track your time <em>in the moment</em>. Our tool helps you document start and end times precisely and deduct breaks correctly, ensuring every minute counts toward your revenue.</p>
        <a href={hubUrl} class="btn btn-primary">Start Tracking Project Time</a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .guide-content {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 2rem auto;
    padding: 0 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .guide-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .breadcrumb {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    background: var(--grad-primary);
    -webkit-background-clip: text;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
  }
  h2 {
    color: var(--primary);
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .content-card {
    padding: 2.5rem;
  }
  .tip-box {
    background: rgba(var(--primary-rgb), 0.1);
    border: 1px solid var(--primary);
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 12px;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding: 1rem 2rem;
    background: var(--grad-primary);
    color: white;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
